Translation patch: keystore2::legacy_blob::LegacyBlobLoader::is_empty_user

Change: keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs:990: each `format!` on this line is replaced, on the same line, by a block that builds the same `String` with `to_owned`, `push_str` and `to_string`: the directory `user_{user}` is built from the literal `user_` and the decimal rendering of the user.
Why: the translation models the arguments of `format!` as `()` (`core::fmt::Arguments` is `Unit` in the Aeneas library), so the translated function tested the same directory for every user. `to_owned`, `push_str` and `to_string` are translated as calls whose results depend on their arguments.
Behaviour: unchanged. The pushed component is the same. `Display` of a string or an integer with no format options writes the same bytes as `push_str` of the string or of the integer's `to_string`. The string is built at the same point and lives at least as long; no panic is added or removed (allocation failure aborts in both).
Classification: B
Assumptions: none.
Obligations: fork === upstream: the rewritten function behaves as the original on every input.
Evidence: an independent equivalence review by three reviewers, accepted on 2 of 3; summarised in formal/EXTRACTION-ISSUES.md.
Independent: yes

diff --git a/keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs b/keystore2/src/legacy_blob.rs
